+## O3 — §3(b)'s "separate per-office cap" removal risks the non-resettable `UPPER_BOUND` and the measured envelope (Act 34 §3(2)–(3), §3(1)(c), §3(5))
+
+**Sources.** Founder `sha256:i_KDrOgIN…`: "If the current Act34 separate caps/attestation machinery makes otherwise authorized ordinary Antonina work impossible… no serial approval or separate office cap unless a real resource constraint justifies one" — the exception is itself the Founder's condition. Act 34 §3(2): `UPPER_BOUND` charges "accumulate on the unchanged 45-day Economy ledger and are never reset by restarting, renaming or expanding a pilot"; §3(1)(c) requires per-request, concurrency, CPU/wall ceilings and a ≤20 s monitor; §3(5) requires a measured envelope and ceilings "at or below that measured envelope and at or below lawful available authority". Bill §4 lists the "non-resettable cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` resource ledger and honest accounting/dispatch ceilings (Act 34 §3(2)–(3))" as preserved.
+
+**Defect.** §3(b) removes "a per-office cap separate from the ordinary resource constraints … when imposed merely as a pre-start permit/dispatch formality." Act 34 §3(1)(c)'s ceilings and §3(5)'s measured envelope are substantive resource constraints, but a reader can characterise them as "separate per-office caps" and a "pre-start" requirement. The bill never says they survive. If the envelope is dropped, four parallel offices can each be "individually compliant" while collectively exhausting the host — the failure mode the Founder flagged in 17:45Z/18:15Z ("actual bounded financial authority"). A4's falsifier (ledger reset by restart/rename/expansion, or office exceeding ordinary aggregate authority without fail-closed suspension) is not closed by §4's prose pointer alone.
+
+**Fix F3 (before ballot).** Add to §4: "Nothing in §3 removes Act 34 §3(1)(c)'s conservative per-request, concurrency, CPU/wall and monitor ceilings, §3(2)'s non-resettable cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` (never reset by restart, rename, re-permitting or expansion), or §3(5)'s measured envelope and its 'at or below lawful available authority' rule. Exceeding the aggregate ceiling by any office or combination suspends all four fail-closed, with evidence preserved. 'Ordinary resource constraints' means these constraints as independently verified on the exact dispatch path, not the absence of a cap."
