+## O7 — "documented real resource constraint or preserved safeguard" is too vague to be auditable; here is falsifiable wording
+
+**Sources.** Bill §3 exception; §5; assumptions A4/A5; Founder 17:52Z "unless a real resource constraint justifies one" and 18:15Z "not a waiver of genuine financial or privacy safeguards."
+
+**Defect.** "Documented" does not say by whom, where, on what bytes, or with what acceptance test. "Justifies" has no standard. A one-line permit comment could assert a "real resource constraint" or cite §4 generically with no numeric envelope, no board review and no verification of the exact bytes. That is unauditable, and it is the hinge on which O1–O4 turn.
+
+**Fix F7 (before ballot).** Replace the §3 exception with: "An item is retained only where, **before any permit issues**, a source-linked record on canonical `main` states: (i) the exact file and field or control retained; (ii) for a resource constraint, the numeric ceiling/envelope and the Economy measurement that makes it binding, or for a preserved safeguard, the exact §4 clause and the byte-level enforcement mechanism; (iii) the named independent verifier (Economy for resource/financial items, Judiciary for privacy, Spying-source and after-start items) and the exact-review disposition; and (iv) the review date. The record must be verified on the exact bytes to be deployed by the gate in clause F2 above. Absent any element, the item is retained by default and dispatch fails closed; no Executive assertion alone satisfies this exception."
+
+---
+
+## O8 — §2(2)'s "tier label is never authority" is correct but incomplete: source-label and route-label laundering is not expressly barred for Spying
+
+**Sources.** Act 34 §3(4); bill §2(2); assumptions A5 ("Spying admits a source outside the code-enforced allowlist, a secret enters a training route, Post is treated as authority").
+
+**Defect.** §2(2) bars a "model-name suffix, tier label, Post sender label or inferred preference" as "enforcement or authority" for **tier claims**. It does not say that a source's own label, an agent output, a publication count or a Post message may not be promoted into a Spying source, a permit, a ballot reason, a Founder communication, or a data route. F4 closes the route half; the source half should be explicit so parity cannot be used to launder an out-of-allowlist source through "ordinary" practice.
+
+**Fix F8 (optional strengthening, recommended before ballot).** Add to §4: "No office may elevate an inferred preference, a source or sender label, an agent output, a publication or a Post message into an authorized Spying source, a Founder communication, a ballot, an instruction, a verified fact, a spending authority or a data route. Publication counts, merges and clean reports are never outcomes."
+
