+## Falsifier symmetry — what would change my verdict
+
+- I move to **YES unchanged** only if the balloted text expressly states F1–F7 as text (not merely relies on §4 pointers), with F4 non-negotiable, and the assumptions schedule is filed with A1–A5 falsifiers keyed to them.
+- I move to **NO** if any prelaunch value/calibration/PROCEED gate returns; if the non-resettable `UPPER_BOUND` or Act 34 §3(1) exact-path tier verification is made resettable or unverifiable; if the 48 h check becomes advisory or re-anchorable; if Iceman/Beam or any training-enabled/region-restricted route is admitted to the shared knowledge-office path without a later exact-author Founder communication or enacted law; if a Spying source outside the code-enforced allowlist is treated as authority; or if ballots are solicited before this finding, a sponsor response, and a filed assumptions schedule exist.
+- I do **not** condition support on a strict per-request billing cap (the Founder relaxed that in the Act 34 line); I condition it on honest labelling and independently **verified** enforceable controls on the exact dispatch path.
